        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.duplication-hit",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "F3 (advisory, verified). Duplication scan (--rust-semantic, 41 needles, 1151/1151 sibling branches) surfaces dense_prefill_chunk_rows (generate_2.rs:1143-1146) next to the pre-existing attention_rows_for (forward_qwen35_cuda_prefill.rs:208-213). The author-flagged difference, num_heads versus heads_per_kv, is CORRECT here rather than merely conservative: the dense path allocates its score scratch as num_heads * rows * total_len (cublas_prefill/attention.rs:361, 542, 776; executor kv_num_heads is the Q-head count per mod.rs:496), so num_heads is the exact multiplier and heads_per_kv would under-budget the buffer by a factor of heads_per_kv. attention_rows_for legitimately uses heads_per_kv because the Qwen3.5 path scores one KV group per pass. prefill_count == 0 returns at generate_2.rs:251 before `(prefill_count - 1) % rows` at 358, so the subtraction cannot underflow. Remaining duplication hits are lexical: half_to_f32 in the new file's test module (f16_iq4xs_dequant.rs:291) mirrors a test-local helper in q5k/dequant.rs and q8_0_dequant.rs, and sibling branches of this same work carry the same new files."
          },
          "locations": [
