      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "mutation.defer-dir-missing",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "F6 (RESOLVED IN DIFF, not open; the x86-main CI failure on head fc88268134). scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh gate() truncated the --defer-unbuilt file (line 47 at fc88268134) before the directory of that file existed. ci/sections.yml:3594 passes --out mutants-gate --defer-unbuilt mutants-gate/not_measured.txt on a fresh checkout, where mutants-gate/ is only made later (mkdir -p on the --out dir), so the redirect failed and the mutants section went RED before any mutant was listed. Reproduced with the pre-fix blob (git show fc88268134:scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh) in a fresh scratch dir: rc=1, pre.sh line 47: mutants-gate/not_measured.txt: No such file or directory, no file written; --defer-unbuilt nodir/x.txt fails the same way. With head 98d7ffb1c7 (one commit, scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh only: mkdir -p of the dirname, then the truncate, lines 47-49) the same two invocations return rc=0 and the file exists. It adds self-test rows defer-into-a-missing-dir and defer-dir-created plus the mutant defer-dir-not-made, killed by the former; the self-test is now PASS with 58 ok rows and 27 killed mutants. The earlier self-test never caught it because every row wrote the deferred file into a directory that already existed. This was a defect of the earlier heads that my round 1 and round 2 reviews missed: both exercised the gate only through its self-test and a stub harness whose --out dir already existed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 44,
                  "endLine": 51
