            "failure_scenario": "Any CI run of the mutants section on a fresh checkout with --defer-unbuilt mutants-gate/not_measured.txt: the redirect fails, the section is RED before mutation starts, and no PR can pass x86-main."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "mutation.harness-gap",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "F2. mutants_diff_gate.sh judge() (line 115) enters the unbuilt-split branch only when missed+timeout exceeds --max-missed. With --max-missed N>0 a NOT_MEASURED (unbuilt, cfg(feature)) survivor within the tolerance is silently counted as tolerated: it is neither deferred to the shard nor reported RED. Measured with a stub cargo: max 0 -> RED with NOT_MEASURED named; max 1 with the same single unbuilt survivor -> `ok every mutant in the diff was caught (or within --max-missed)`. CI defaults MUTANTS_MAX_MISSED to 0 (sections.yml:3172), so an operator has to raise the variable; and the committed self-test set (26 mutants) has no row for it, which is why it survived. Fix: run unbuilt_split before the threshold test and defer or RED the unbuilt set irrespective of max."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 115,
                  "endLine": 134
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "scripts/mutants_diff_gate.sh",
              "--max-missed",
              "1",
              "(stub cargo: /mnt/nvme-raid0/tmp/ec-review-target/loop/cargo)"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "d1c57976ec4ce3b2f75f32584e0635692119a0d72609640930c456df7e4aa2a2",
            "failure_scenario": "An operator sets MUTANTS_MAX_MISSED=1 to land a diff with one legitimate surviving CPU mutant; a cfg(feature=cuda) survivor in the same diff is then absorbed into the tolerance and reported as measured-and-tolerated, never deferred to mutants-cuda."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "mutation.vacuous-skip",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "F5. prefill_refusal_tests_4621 (prefill.rs:1626-1660) and dequant_dispatch_tests_4621 (gdn_prefill_ops.rs:594-610) return early when no CUDA device exists (`let Some(mut exec) = executor() else { return }`). On the CPU workspace-test job they pass without asserting anything (L25: a skip is not_measured, never pass). The comment states the intent: under the GPU mutants-cuda shard a skip leaves the mutant alive and the shard RED. Acceptable as designed now that F1 is fixed in this head: the gate reads the shard result, so a skip leaves the mutant alive and the shard RED."
          },
